# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .prettierignore — RWA-Vault
#
# Tells `pnpm format` and `pnpm format:check` which paths to skip.
# Everything listed here is either machine-generated (reformatting it would
# create noisy diffs on every rebuild) or managed by a different formatter
# (e.g. forge fmt for Solidity).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── JavaScript/TypeScript build output ───────────────────────────────────
# Compiled .js files in dist/ and build/ are regenerated by `tsc` — formatting
# them would be immediately overwritten on the next build.
node_modules/
dist/
build/

# ─── Package manager lockfile ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# pnpm-lock.yaml is machine-generated and must not be reformatted. Prettier
# would normalise whitespace and break the lockfile's integrity hash.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# ─── Foundry artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Solidity compilation output (ABI JSON, bytecode) — machine-generated.
contracts/out/
# Forge compilation cache — binary files, not formattable.
contracts/cache/
# Deployment broadcast logs — JSON artefacts from `forge script`. These are
# an audit trail and should be committed as-is, not reformatted.
contracts/broadcast/
# Git submodule dependencies (forge-std, openzeppelin) — third-party code
# that we don't own and shouldn't reformat.
contracts/lib/

# ─── Rust / WASM output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# wasm-pack output for the pq-core browser build — generated .js/.ts glue code.
packages/pq-core/pkg/
# Cargo build output (native compilation of the Rust pq-core crate).
target/

# ─── Vendored PQClean ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Third-party C at a pinned upstream commit, plus a generated PROVENANCE.md
# whose SHA-256/Git-object manifest is verified byte-for-byte against that
# commit. Reformatting it would invalidate the manifest and fail
# scripts/verify-vendor.py. The tree is regenerated by scripts/vendor-pqclean.py
# and must never be edited by any tool.
packages/pq-core/native/vendor/
